  <working-storage><![CDATA[       01 WS-H                                   GLOBAL    PIC S9(9)    COMP-5.
       01 WS-N                                   GLOBAL    PIC S9(9)    COMP-5.
       01 WS-FS                                  GLOBAL    PIC XX.
       01 WS-ROW                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(1600).
       01 WS-SQL                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(8000).
       01 WS-WHERE                               GLOBAL    PIC X(3000).
       01 WS-P                                   GLOBAL    PIC 9(5).
       01 WS-VIEW                                GLOBAL    PIC X    VALUE "D".
       01 WS-METRIC                              GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 1.
       01 WS-ACUM                                GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 1.
       01 WS-LEVELS-OPEN                         GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-LOADED                              GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-PAGE                                GLOBAL    PIC 9(5)    VALUE 1.
       01 WS-PAGES                               GLOBAL    PIC 9(5)    VALUE 1.
       01 WS-PSIZE                               GLOBAL    PIC 9(4)    VALUE 300.
       01 WS-UNIV                                GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-CATCNT                              GLOBAL    PIC 99    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-FV                                  GLOBAL    PIC 9(15)V99.
       01 WS-FC                                  GLOBAL    PIC 9(12).
       01 WS-FP                                  GLOBAL    PIC 9(3)V9.
       01 WS-FT                                  GLOBAL    PIC X(24).
       01 WS-CHK                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(1200).
       01 WS-IN                                  GLOBAL    PIC X(1500).
       01 WS-SM                                  GLOBAL    PIC X    VALUE SPACE.
       01 WS-SMX                                 GLOBAL    PIC X    VALUE SPACE.
       01 WS-ALL-N                               GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-ALL-C                               GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-TERM                                GLOBAL    PIC X(80).
       01 WS-LAST-N                              GLOBAL    PIC X(80).
       01 WS-LAST-C                              GLOBAL    PIC X(80).
       01 WS-PAT                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(90).
       01 WS-ONE                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(200).
       01 WS-ESC                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(420).
       01 WS-BIG                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(24000).
       01 WS-BPTR                                GLOBAL    PIC 9(5).
       01 WS-SMN                                 GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-SMK                                 GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-T0                                  GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-ELAPSED                             GLOBAL    PIC S9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-STAGE                               GLOBAL    PIC 99    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-COLOR-DATA                          GLOBAL.
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#3E7BE8".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#F5A524".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#22C3D6".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#8B5CF6".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#2FBF71".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#F0527A".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#FF7A45".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#394670".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#B5D334".
           05 FILLER                             PIC    X(7)    VALUE "#C9D3E6".
       01 WS-COLOR-TAB                           REDEFINES    WS-COLOR-DATA    GLOBAL.
           05 WS-COLOR                           PIC    X(7)    OCCURS 10.
       01 WS-CAT-TAB                             GLOBAL.
           05 WS-CAT-ROW                         OCCURS    10.
               10 WS-CAT-NAME                    PIC    X(24).
               10 WS-CAT-CNT                     PIC    9(9).
               10 WS-CAT-PL                      PIC    9(15)V99.
               10 WS-CAT-COT                     PIC    9(12).
               10 WS-CAT-USED                    PIC    9.
       01 WS-TOT                                 GLOBAL.
           05 WS-T-CNT                           PIC    9(9).
           05 WS-T-PL                            PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 WS-T-COT                           PIC    9(12).
           05 WS-T-PLN                           PIC    9(9).
           05 WS-T-MAX                           PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 WS-T-YMAX                          PIC    9(4).
           05 WS-T-CLS                           PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 WS-T-SUB                           PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 WS-T-TOPN                          PIC    X(60).
       01 WS-N2-TAB                              GLOBAL.
           05 WS-N2-ROW                          OCCURS    10.
               10 WS-N2-NAME                     PIC    X(24).
               10 WS-N2-CNT                      PIC    9(9).
       01 WS-N2-TOTAL                            GLOBAL    PIC 9(9).
       01 WS-BIN-TAB                             GLOBAL.
           05 WS-BIN-CNT                         PIC    9(9)    OCCURS 5.
       01 WS-TOP-TAB                             GLOBAL.
           05 WS-TOP-ROW                         OCCURS    4.
      *> X(44), not the desktop's X(40): the Backend cuts the name at 40 bytes and, when the
      *> cut falls inside a letter, sends the cut text + U+FFFD (what the desktop shows). A
      *> browser module refuses a caption that is not valid UTF-8, so the form must not cut
      *> that character again.
               10 WS-TOP-NAME                    PIC    X(44).
               10 WS-TOP-PL                      PIC    9(15)V99.
       01 WS-TOP-N                               GLOBAL    PIC 9.
       01 WS-RANK-TAB                            GLOBAL.
           05 WS-RANK                            PIC    99    OCCURS 10.
       01 WS-TOP3                                GLOBAL.
           05 WS-TOP3-IDX                        PIC    99    OCCURS 3.
       01 WS-YR-TAB                              GLOBAL.
           05 WS-YR-MIN                          PIC    9(4).
           05 WS-YR                              OCCURS    12.
               10 WS-YR-NUM                      PIC    9(4).
               10 WS-YA-CNT                      PIC    9(9).
               10 WS-YA-PL                       PIC    9(15)V99.
               10 WS-YA-COT                      PIC    9(12).
               10 WS-YS                          OCCURS    3.
                   15 WS-YS-CNT                  PIC    9(9).
                   15 WS-YS-PL                   PIC    9(15)V99.
                   15 WS-YS-COT                  PIC    9(12).
       01 WS-OFF-TAB                             GLOBAL.
           05 WS-OA-CNT                          PIC    9(9).
           05 WS-OA-PL                           PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 WS-OA-COT                          PIC    9(12).
           05 WS-OS                              OCCURS    3.
               10 WS-OS-CNT                      PIC    9(9).
               10 WS-OS-PL                       PIC    9(15)V99.
               10 WS-OS-COT                      PIC    9(12).
       01 WS-BP                                  GLOBAL    PIC X(12).
       01 WS-CHARTS                              GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-DSTAGE                              GLOBAL    PIC 99    VALUE 1.
       01 WS-GSTAGE                              GLOBAL    PIC 99    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-T0G                                 GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
      *> The data tier of the web form. A browser module holds no database: every question the
      *> desktop asks DB-1 is asked of a Backend program (backend/src/fund-*.cbl) with
      *> CALL ... WITH WEBSOCKET LINKAGE. The form sends the filter as VALUES (FLT-REQ) and reads
      *> the answer groups below; the SQL is fixed inside the programs. The layouts are the ones
      *> of backend/COPYBOOKS (req-*.cpy, res-*.cpy): the member names and sizes are the wire.
      *> FLT-NAME-TERM / FLT-CAT-TERM: the first 80 bytes of the typed text, as the desktop's
      *> WS-TERM (PIC X(80)) keeps them, plus the rest of a letter the 80th byte falls into (at
      *> most 3 bytes, TERM-CUT): a request must be UTF-8. The Backend cuts them to 80 bytes.
      *> FLT-NAME-FLAGS: the ticked company names, byte k = "1" for the name of fund id k
      *> (NAM-ID); the desktop's table pick has no limit, and one byte per fund lets every
      *> name be ticked within the 64 KiB of a call.
       01 FLT-REQ                                GLOBAL.
           05 FLT-NAME-TERM                      PIC    X(83).
           05 FLT-NAME-N                         PIC    9(5).
           05 FLT-NAME-FLAGS                     PIC    X(50000).
           05 FLT-CAT-TERM                       PIC    X(83).
           05 FLT-CAT-N                          PIC    99.
           05 FLT-CAT-PICK                       PIC    X(60)
                                                 OCCURS 0 TO 10 DEPENDING ON FLT-CAT-N.
           05 FLT-DATE-FROM                      PIC    X(10).
           05 FLT-DATE-TO                        PIC    X(10).
           05 FLT-PL-FROM                        PIC    9(9).
           05 FLT-PL-TO                          PIC    9(9).
           05 FLT-N2-N                           PIC    99.
           05 FLT-N2-PICK                        PIC    X(60)
                                                 OCCURS 0 TO 32 DEPENDING ON FLT-N2-N.
           05 FLT-N3-N                           PIC    99.
           05 FLT-N3-PICK                        PIC    X(60)
                                                 OCCURS 0 TO 64 DEPENDING ON FLT-N3-N.
      *> FLS-REQ: the filter of the LAST Apply. The desktop pages and re-sorts the grid with the
      *> WS-WHERE of the last APPLY-FILTERS; FLT-SAVE keeps it here, FLT-RESTORE puts it back.
       01 FLS-REQ                                GLOBAL.
           05 FLS-NAME-TERM                      PIC    X(83).
           05 FLS-NAME-N                         PIC    9(5).
           05 FLS-NAME-FLAGS                     PIC    X(50000).
           05 FLS-CAT-TERM                       PIC    X(83).
           05 FLS-CAT-N                          PIC    99.
           05 FLS-CAT-PICK                       PIC    X(60)    OCCURS 10.
           05 FLS-DATE-FROM                      PIC    X(10).
           05 FLS-DATE-TO                        PIC    X(10).
           05 FLS-PL-FROM                        PIC    9(9).
           05 FLS-PL-TO                          PIC    9(9).
           05 FLS-N2-N                           PIC    99.
           05 FLS-N2-PICK                        PIC    X(60)    OCCURS 32.
           05 FLS-N3-N                           PIC    99.
           05 FLS-N3-PICK                        PIC    X(60)    OCCURS 64.
       01 GRD-REQ                                GLOBAL.
           05 GRD-ORDER                          PIC    X(40).
           05 GRD-OFFSET                         PIC    9(9).
           05 GRD-LIMIT                          PIC    9(4).
       01 NAM-REQ                                GLOBAL.
           05 NAM-BOX                            PIC    X.
       01 INI-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 INI-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 INI-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 INI-LOAD                           PIC    X(8).
           05 INI-LINES                          PIC    9(6).
           05 INI-UNIV                           PIC    9(9).
           05 INI-REFDATE                        PIC    X(10).
           05 INI-CAT-N                          PIC    99.
           05 INI-CAT-NAME                       PIC    X(24)    OCCURS 10.
           05 INI-N2-TOTAL                       PIC    9(4).
           05 INI-N2-N                           PIC    99.
           05 INI-N2-NAME                        PIC    X(60)
                                                 OCCURS 0 TO 64 DEPENDING ON INI-N2-N.
           05 INI-N3-TOTAL                       PIC    9(4).
           05 INI-N3-N                           PIC    99.
           05 INI-N3-NAME                        PIC    X(60)
                                                 OCCURS 0 TO 64 DEPENDING ON INI-N3-N.
       01 TOT-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 TOT-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 TOT-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 TOT-CNT                            PIC    9(9).
           05 TOT-PL                             PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 TOT-COT                            PIC    9(12).
           05 TOT-PLN                            PIC    9(9).
           05 TOT-MAX                            PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 TOT-YMAX                           PIC    9(4).
           05 TOT-CLS                            PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 TOT-SUB                            PIC    9(15)V99.
       01 CAR-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 CAR-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 CAR-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 CAR-N                              PIC    99.
           05 CAR-NAME                           PIC    X(24)    OCCURS 10.
           05 CAR-CNT                            PIC    9(9)    OCCURS 10.
           05 CAR-PL                             PIC    9(15)V99    OCCURS 10.
           05 CAR-COT                            PIC    9(12)    OCCURS 10.
       01 N2R-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 N2R-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 N2R-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 N2R-NAME                           PIC    X(24)    OCCURS 10.
           05 N2R-CNT                            PIC    9(9)    OCCURS 10.
           05 N2R-TOTAL                          PIC    9(9).
       01 BIN-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 BIN-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 BIN-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 BIN-CNT                            PIC    9(9)    OCCURS 5.
       01 TOP-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 TOP-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 TOP-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 TOP-N                              PIC    9.
      *> TOP-NAME / RAD-NAME are 4 bytes wider than the Backend's: a name cut at 40 (160)
      *> bytes inside a letter travels as the cut text + U+FFFD (3 bytes), the replacement
      *> character the desktop shows at the end of such a name; WS-TOP-NAME / WS-RN cut it
      *> back to 40 (160) bytes as the desktop does.
           05 TOP-NAME                           PIC    X(44)    OCCURS 4.
           05 TOP-PL                             PIC    9(15)V99    OCCURS 4.
       01 YRS-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 YRS-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 YRS-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 YRS-TOP3                           PIC    99    OCCURS 3.
           05 YRS-MIN                            PIC    9(4).
           05 YRS-YEAR                           OCCURS    12.
               10 YRS-NUM                        PIC    9(4).
               10 YRS-A-CNT                      PIC    9(9).
               10 YRS-A-PL                       PIC    9(15)V99.
               10 YRS-A-COT                      PIC    9(12).
               10 YRS-S                          OCCURS    3.
                   15 YRS-S-CNT                  PIC    9(9).
                   15 YRS-S-PL                   PIC    9(15)V99.
                   15 YRS-S-COT                  PIC    9(12).
           05 YRS-OA-CNT                         PIC    9(9).
           05 YRS-OA-PL                          PIC    9(15)V99.
           05 YRS-OA-COT                         PIC    9(12).
           05 YRS-OS                             OCCURS    3.
               10 YRS-OS-CNT                     PIC    9(9).
               10 YRS-OS-PL                      PIC    9(15)V99.
               10 YRS-OS-COT                     PIC    9(12).
       01 GRD-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 GRD-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 GRD-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 GRD-N                              PIC    9(4).
           05 GRD-MORE                           PIC    X.
           05 GRD-ROW                            PIC    X(400)
                                                 OCCURS 0 TO 150 DEPENDING ON GRD-N.
       01 NAM-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 NAM-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 NAM-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 NAM-KEY                            PIC    X(240).
           05 NAM-MATCHES                        PIC    9(9).
           05 NAM-LISTED                         PIC    9(4).
           05 NAM-ROW                            OCCURS 0 TO 150 DEPENDING ON NAM-LISTED.
               10 NAM-NAME                       PIC    X(210).
               10 NAM-ID                         PIC    9(9).
               10 NAM-TICK                       PIC    9.
       01 RAD-RES                                GLOBAL.
           05 RAD-STATUS                         PIC    X(8).
           05 RAD-MESSAGE                        PIC    X(160).
           05 RAD-NM                             PIC    9.
           05 RAD-NAME                           PIC    X(164)    OCCURS 3.
           05 RAD-RV                             OCCURS    3.
               10 RAD-CNT                        PIC    9(9)    OCCURS 10.
      *> The picker state the desktop keeps in its SQL tables pick and vis, kept here per page:
      *> PK-* the names ticked in each box (pick: 'N' company names as one byte per fund id,
      *> "1" at the id FUND-NAMES gave the name, as many as the data holds; 'C' categories by
      *> name), VS-* the names the open list shows (vis) and, for 'N', their ids.
       01 PK-TAB                                 GLOBAL.
           05 PK-N-N                             PIC    9(5)    VALUE 0.
           05 PK-N-FLAGS                         PIC    X(50000)    VALUE SPACES.
           05 PK-C-N                             PIC    99    VALUE 0.
           05 PK-C-NAME                          PIC    X(60)    OCCURS 10.
       01 VS-TAB                                 GLOBAL.
           05 VS-N-N                             PIC    9(3)    VALUE 0.
           05 VS-N-ROW                           OCCURS 150.
               10 VS-N-NAME                      PIC    X(210).
               10 VS-N-ID                        PIC    9(9).
           05 VS-C-N                             PIC    99    VALUE 0.
           05 VS-C-NAME                          PIC    X(60)    OCCURS 10.
      *> TERM-CUT: WS-CUT-IN = a typed text (its first 84 bytes), WS-CUT-OUT = what travels.
       01 WS-CUT-IN                              GLOBAL    PIC X(84).
       01 WS-CUT-OUT                             GLOBAL    PIC X(83).
      *> The header line. WS-STATUS-TXT = what the desktop's own flow wrote there (LOAD-DIMS, or
      *> INIT-DB without data); a failed Backend call shows its error instead (BACKEND-FAIL,
      *> WS-BE-SHOWN = 1) until a later flow of calls runs without a failure (BE-FLOW-END).
      *> WS-BE-FAILS counts failed calls; WS-BE-MARK = the count when the outermost flow began;
      *> WS-BE-DEPTH = flows running (Apply runs the grid's flow inside its own).
       01 WS-STATUS-TXT                          GLOBAL    PIC X(120)    VALUE SPACES.
       01 WS-BE-SHOWN                            GLOBAL    PIC 9    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-BE-FAILS                            GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-BE-MARK                             GLOBAL    PIC 9(9)    VALUE 0.
       01 WS-BE-DEPTH                            GLOBAL    PIC 9(4)    VALUE 0.
      *> How the last Backend call went: BE-PROG the program, BE-STATUS its status word (or the
      *> class of a failed call), BE-CODE / BE-MSG what COBOL::"WS-LAST-ERROR" or the program said.
       01 BE-PROG                                GLOBAL    PIC X(12).
       01 BE-STATUS                              GLOBAL    PIC X(16).
       01 BE-CLASS                               GLOBAL    PIC X(16).
       01 BE-CODE                                GLOBAL    PIC 9(9).
       01 BE-MSG                                 GLOBAL    PIC X(200).
]]></working-storage>
