    <Event name="onTextChanged" paragraph="TXT-NOME--ONTEXTCHANGED"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> ENSURE-INIT: gives the page the desktop's start-up state when FUND-INIT failed.
           *> Uses:   WS-LOADED and INI-STATUS (nothing is done once the database answered, nor
           *>         without data); FLS-REQ, the filter of the last Apply (never the controls'
           *>         unapplied edits).
           *> Result: after a late Backend start: the header line, LST-N2 / LST-N3, the
           *>         dashboard, the Dados cards and the grid as the desktop shows them after
           *>         start-up; while the Backend is still down, its error in the header.

           CALL    "ENSURE-INIT"
           SET     WS-SMX                        TO    "N"

           *> SM-TYPED: reacts to typing in a filter box: opens or refreshes its search dropdown.
           *> Uses:   WS-SMX = "N" (set just above), TXT-NOME::Text, WS-LAST-N (the last term
           *>         handled for this box) and WS-SM, which decides between SM-OPEN (WS-SM differs
           *>         from WS-SMX) and SM-REFRESH (it equals it).
           *> Result: Text equal to WS-LAST-N: nothing else happens (WS-TERM = the text). Otherwise
           *>         WS-LAST-N = the text and the names dropdown is opened (SM-OPEN) or, if already
           *>         open, refreshed (SM-REFRESH). Either way WS-TERM ends as the folded text (no
           *>         accents, upper case) and WS-PAT as its LIKE pattern (NORM-TERM), and LST-SM,
           *>         its CheckedItems, WS-SMN (all the matches), WS-SMK (at most 150 names are
           *>         listed) and LBL-SM-INFO::Caption are rebuilt. SM-OPEN also sets WS-SM = "N",
           *>         closes the Levels popup if it was open, recomputes the layout and sets
           *>         POPUP-SEARCH::Visible = TRUE.

           CALL    "SM-TYPED"
]]></Event>
    <Event name="onEnterPressed" paragraph="TXT-NOME--ONENTERPRESSED"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> SM-CLOSE: closes the search dropdown when one is open.
           *> Uses:   WS-SM ("N" or "C" while a dropdown is open, SPACE otherwise).
           *> Result: Only when WS-SM was not SPACE: WS-SM = SPACE and POPUP-SEARCH::Visible =
           *>         FALSE. Otherwise nothing changes.

           CALL    "SM-CLOSE"

           *> APPLY-FILTERS: re-runs every query and repaints the dashboard, the charts and the grid
           *> for the current filters; it exits at once while WS-LOADED = 0.
           *> Uses:   TXT-NOME::Text as typed, the other filter controls, the picks kept in PK-TAB
           *>         and the Todos flags WS-ALL-N / WS-ALL-C (in Todos mode the picks are ignored
           *>         and the typed text is used).
           *> Result: WS-PAGE = 1; FLT-REQ rebuilt from the controls; the Q-* steps recompute the
           *>         totals (WS-T-*), WS-CAT-*, WS-RANK, WS-N2-*, WS-BIN-CNT, WS-TOP-* and the year
           *>         tables; the PAINT-* steps repaint the KPI card, the charts, the top-4 list
           *>         with the Classe / Subclasse bars, the Dados cards and the metric buttons;
           *>         GRD-FUNDOS shows page 1, with its caption LBL-GRID-S, the page label LBL-PAGE
           *>         and BTN-PREV / BTN-NEXT enabled to match.

           CALL    "APPLY-FILTERS"
]]></Event>
    <Event name="onEscapePressed" paragraph="TXT-NOME--ONESCAPEPRESSED"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> ENSURE-INIT: gives the page the desktop's start-up state when FUND-INIT failed.
           *> Uses:   WS-LOADED and INI-STATUS (nothing is done once the database answered, nor
           *>         without data); FLS-REQ, the filter of the last Apply (never the controls'
           *>         unapplied edits).
           *> Result: after a late Backend start: the header line, LST-N2 / LST-N3, the
           *>         dashboard, the Dados cards and the grid as the desktop shows them after
           *>         start-up; while the Backend is still down, its error in the header.

           CALL    "ENSURE-INIT"

           *> SM-CLOSE: closes the search dropdown when one is open.
           *> Uses:   WS-SM ("N" or "C" while a dropdown is open, SPACE otherwise).
           *> Result: Only when WS-SM was not SPACE: WS-SM = SPACE and POPUP-SEARCH::Visible =
           *>         FALSE. The filter is not applied.

           CALL    "SM-CLOSE"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
