    <Property name="ScaleFont">1</Property>
    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-NM-TG--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> ENSURE-INIT: gives the page the desktop's start-up state when FUND-INIT failed.
           *> Uses:   WS-LOADED and INI-STATUS (nothing is done once the database answered, nor
           *>         without data); FLS-REQ, the filter of the last Apply (never the controls'
           *>         unapplied edits).
           *> Result: after a late Backend start: the header line, LST-N2 / LST-N3, the
           *>         dashboard, the Dados cards and the grid as the desktop shows them after
           *>         start-up; while the Backend is still down, its error in the header.

           CALL    "ENSURE-INIT"
           IF    WS-SM = "N"

               *> SM-CLOSE: closes the search dropdown when one is open.
               *> Uses:   WS-SM, which is "N" here: the names dropdown is open and the button
               *>         toggles it.
               *> Result: WS-SM = SPACE and POPUP-SEARCH::Visible = FALSE.

               CALL    "SM-CLOSE"
           ELSE
               SET     WS-SMX                    TO    "N"

               *> SM-OPEN: opens the search dropdown (layer POPUP-SEARCH) for the filter box named
               *> in WS-SMX.
               *> Uses:   WS-SMX = "N" (set just above). Caller's test (not read by SM-OPEN): WS-SM
               *>         is not "N", so no dropdown, or the category one, is open.
               *> Result: WS-SM = "N"; the Levels popup is closed if it was open (CLOSE-LEVELS);
               *>         LBL-SM-T::Caption = "Nome comercial  ·  marque os fundos que quer ver";
               *>         the layout is recomputed (SET-FILT-HEIGHT places the search card);
               *>         SM-REFRESH fills LST-SM for the current TXT-NOME::Text (at most 150
               *>         names), sets WS-SMN (all matches) and WS-SMK, sets LST-SM::CheckedItems
               *>         (SM-TICKS) and sets LBL-SM-INFO::Caption (SM-INFO); POPUP-SEARCH::Visible
               *>         = TRUE.

               CALL    "SM-OPEN"
           END-IF
]]></Event>
  </Control>
