    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-NEXT--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> ENSURE-INIT: gives the page the desktop's start-up state when FUND-INIT failed.
           *> Uses:   WS-LOADED and INI-STATUS (nothing is done once the database answered, nor
           *>         without data); FLS-REQ, the filter of the last Apply (never the controls'
           *>         unapplied edits).
           *> Result: after a late Backend start: the header line, LST-N2 / LST-N3, the
           *>         dashboard, the Dados cards and the grid as the desktop shows them after
           *>         start-up; while the Backend is still down, its error in the header.

           CALL    "ENSURE-INIT"
           IF    WS-PAGE < WS-PAGES
               ADD    1 TO WS-PAGE

               *> REFRESH-GRID: reloads the grid page and its captions.
               *> Uses:   WS-PAGE, just increased by 1 (it was below WS-PAGES), CMB-ORDER::Value,
               *>         and FLS-REQ and WS-T-CNT as the last APPLY-FILTERS left them (the filters
               *>         are not re-run here).
               *> Result: GRD-FUNDOS holds the next page; LBL-GRID-S, LBL-PAGE, BTN-PREV and
               *>         BTN-NEXT match that page (BTN-NEXT is disabled on the last page).

               CALL    "REFRESH-GRID"
           END-IF
]]></Event>
