    <Event name="onItemChecked" paragraph="LST-SM--ONITEMCHECKED"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> ENSURE-INIT: gives the page the desktop's start-up state when FUND-INIT failed.
           *> Uses:   WS-LOADED and INI-STATUS (nothing is done once the database answered, nor
           *>         without data); FLS-REQ, the filter of the last Apply (never the controls'
           *>         unapplied edits).
           *> Result: after a late Backend start: the header line, LST-N2 / LST-N3, the
           *>         dashboard, the Dados cards and the grid as the desktop shows them after
           *>         start-up; while the Backend is still down, its error in the header.

           CALL    "ENSURE-INIT"

           *> SM-CHECKED: applies a tick change of LST-SM: stores the ticked names, updates Todos
           *> mode and the kept picks.
           *> Uses:   LST-SM::CheckedItems (the ticked rows, LF-separated), WS-SM ("N" or "C"), the
           *>         Todos flag WS-ALL-N / WS-ALL-C as it was before the click, and VS-TAB.
           *> Result: table chk = the ticked names other than "Todos" (that row only sets WS-TODOS);
           *>         the names kept for WS-SM (PK-TAB) and the Todos flag updated to the new ticks; then
           *>         LST-SM::CheckedItems is rewritten from the new state (SM-TICKS: all rows in
           *>         Todos mode, else the listed names found in pick), LBL-SM-INFO::Caption gets
           *>         the new message (SM-INFO) and the captions of LBL-F-NOME and LBL-F-CAT are
           *>         recomputed (SM-CAPTIONS). The filter is not applied yet.

           CALL    "SM-CHECKED"
]]></Event>
    <Event name="onEscapePressed" paragraph="LST-SM--ONESCAPEPRESSED"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           *> ENSURE-INIT: gives the page the desktop's start-up state when FUND-INIT failed.
           *> Uses:   WS-LOADED and INI-STATUS (nothing is done once the database answered, nor
           *>         without data); FLS-REQ, the filter of the last Apply (never the controls'
           *>         unapplied edits).
           *> Result: after a late Backend start: the header line, LST-N2 / LST-N3, the
           *>         dashboard, the Dados cards and the grid as the desktop shows them after
           *>         start-up; while the Backend is still down, its error in the header.

           CALL    "ENSURE-INIT"

           *> SM-CLOSE: closes the search dropdown when one is open.
           *> Uses:   WS-SM ("N" or "C" while a dropdown is open, SPACE otherwise).
           *> Result: Only when WS-SM was not SPACE: WS-SM = SPACE and POPUP-SEARCH::Visible =
           *>         FALSE. The filter is not applied; the picks made stay in PK-TAB.

           CALL    "SM-CLOSE"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
